<?php declare(strict_types=1); return [['title'=>'What Is a Computer?','slug'=>'what-is-a-computer','content_html'=>'<h2>What is a computer?</h2><p>A computer is an electronic device that accepts data, processes it according to instructions, stores information, and produces useful results. Computers are used for communication, education, business, design, programming and many everyday tasks.</p><h3>Four basic functions</h3><ul><li><strong>Input:</strong> entering data with a keyboard, mouse, camera or other device.</li><li><strong>Processing:</strong> the processor works with instructions and data.</li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> information can be saved for later use.</li><li><strong>Output:</strong> results can appear on a screen, printer or other device.</li></ul><div class="alert alert-primary"><strong>Practice:</strong> Identify one input, processing, storage and output example on your own computer.</div>'],['title'=>'Computer Hardware and Software','slug'=>'computer-hardware-and-software','content_html'=>'<h2>Hardware and software</h2><p><strong>Hardware</strong> means the physical parts of a computer that you can touch, such as the keyboard, monitor, memory and storage drive.</p><p><strong>Software</strong> consists of programs and instructions that tell hardware what to do. Operating systems and applications are common examples.</p><h3>Simple rule</h3><p>Hardware is the equipment; software provides the instructions. They work together to perform useful tasks.</p><div class="alert alert-primary"><strong>Practice:</strong> Make two lists of five hardware devices and five software applications you use.</div>'],['title'=>'Files and Folders','slug'=>'files-and-folders','content_html'=>'<h2>Managing files and folders</h2><p>Files store information such as documents, images, videos and programs. Folders help organize related files so they can be found quickly.</p><h3>Good organization</h3><ol><li>Create folders with clear names.</li><li>Use meaningful filenames.</li><li>Keep related files together.</li><li>Back up important information.</li></ol><p>A simple folder structure makes searching and sharing much easier.</p><div class="alert alert-primary"><strong>Practice:</strong> Create a folder called <code>Learning</code> and inside it create folders for Documents, Images and Projects.</div>'],['title'=>'Keyboard and Mouse Basics','slug'=>'keyboard-and-mouse-basics','content_html'=>'<h2>Keyboard and mouse basics</h2><p>The keyboard is used to enter text and commands, while a mouse or touchpad helps you point, select, drag and interact with items on screen.</p><h3>Useful shortcuts</h3><ul><li><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>C</kbd> — Copy</li><li><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>V</kbd> — Paste</li><li><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>X</kbd> — Cut</li><li><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Z</kbd> — Undo</li><li><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>S</kbd> — Save</li></ul><div class="alert alert-primary"><strong>Practice:</strong> Open a text editor and practice each shortcut with a short paragraph.</div>'],['title'=>'Internet and Web Basics','slug'=>'internet-and-web-basics','content_html'=>'<h2>Internet and the web</h2><p>The internet is a global network of connected devices. The World Wide Web is a service that lets people access linked pages and resources through browsers.</p><h3>Important terms</h3><ul><li><strong>Browser:</strong> software used to access websites.</li><li><strong>Website:</strong> a collection of related web pages and resources.</li><li><strong>URL:</strong> an address used to locate a web resource.</li><li><strong>Search engine:</strong> a service that helps find information online.</li></ul><div class="alert alert-primary"><strong>Practice:</strong> Open your browser, identify the URL of the current page, and explain which part identifies the website.</div>']];